ticas, ya que puede deberse a factores como precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. El límite legal no es un indicador de irregularidad en sí mismo.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden necesidades similares. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con presupuestos cerrados o fechas de alta demanda.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 47 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 13.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.4 to 5.3. December accounts for 4% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 3% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 39 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,499.89 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows a pattern of contracts just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices could be standard, budgets fixed, or needs separate. Statistical trends don't indicate improper actions by the body or contractors.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what was purchased and the reason for the amount. Review the dates and distribution of contracts to see if they align with the body's needs. Look at awardee A's contracts to determine if they repeat the same type of service or supply.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["tOLkLduXDTEtm4eBPtV6eQ%3D%3D","GRIv7fJTsKiP%2Bo96UAV7cQ%3D%3D","DT9tANmd6sjpxJFXpLZ%2B2A%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}